---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy notice for studiobdy.com: no cookies, no analytics, and your email is used only to reply to you."
>
  <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 32px">
    <div class="container stack gap-m">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 56px)">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lead">This site is a plain information site. It is short on privacy implications and this notice is short to match.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 24px">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>studiobdy.com sets no cookies and runs no analytics or advertising scripts. There is nothing to consent to, so there is no banner.</p>
      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>The typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts. When a page loads, your browser requests the font files from Google's servers, which see your IP address as part of that request. Google states that it does not use these requests for tracking. If you would rather avoid this, your browser's content blocker can block fonts.googleapis.com and the site remains readable in your system font.</p>
      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log IP addresses of visitors for security purposes, as described in <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection" rel="noopener">GitHub's documentation</a>. Studio BDY does not receive or use those logs.</p>
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>If you email lee@studiobdy.com, your name, address and message are used to reply to you and to carry on the conversation you started. They are kept in Studio BDY's mailbox for as long as that conversation, and any engagement that follows, needs them, and are not shared with anyone else or used for marketing.</p>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask what personal data Studio BDY holds about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and complain to the Information Commissioner's Office. The data controller is Studio BDY Ltd, 38 Dollar Street, Cirencester, GL7 2AN. Email lee@studiobdy.com with any request.</p>
      <p class="small muted">Last updated 29 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
